### Universal Secure PDF Verification System API Tests (Public Server Mode)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Root Server Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### 2. Upload & Stamp Academic PDF Document (Public Upload)
# NOTE: To run this test in VS Code Rest Client, you must have the file "test-sample.pdf" in the same folder.
# We generated it at d:/QR-Verification/server/test-sample.pdf.
# @name uploadDoc
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/documents/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test-sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./test-sample.pdf
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="documentType"

Academic
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="studentName"

Guru N
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="rollNumber"

ROLL-2026-9051
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="institution"

Guru Academy
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="course"

Computer Science and Engineering
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="gradeCgpa"

9.8/10
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="yearOfPassing"

2026
--boundary--

### Save Document ID from Upload response
@documentId = {{uploadDoc.response.body.data.documentId}}

### 3. Get List of Stamped Documents (Public Listing)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/documents?page=1&limit=10
Accept: application/json

### 4. Get Specific Document Detail & Log audits (Public Lookup)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/documents/{{documentId}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. Public Verification of Active Document by ID (Public Access)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/verify/{{documentId}}
Accept: application/json

### 6. Public Verification of Non-existent Document ID (Public Access)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/verify/DOC-2026-9999
Accept: application/json

### 7. Public Revocation (Anyone can revoke in public-only mode)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/documents/{{documentId}}/revoke
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Student transcript revised after error detection."
}

### 8. Public Verification after Document Revocation (Public Access)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/verify/{{documentId}}
Accept: application/json
